## Corrected 2026-09-07 evening — commentary came back

The first cut of this redesign also removed the Email/WhatsApp digests and any morning assessment, folding "new task identification" into Track C's intake pass and calling that sufficient. It wasn't — Alex's words, on the first real run: **"the daily note has lost some of its charm — it needs more detail and at least *some* commentary."** Facts-only was 2.7 KB; the old note with asides and digests was 4.7 KB, and the gap was exactly the judgement the audit had cut. Track C2 (above) is the fix: a second, separate background subagent scoped to a restricted slice of the brief (~75 KB, not the full ~150 KB) so the original one-Haiku-call latency problem doesn't come back — commentary is now clearly commentary (its own subagent, its own instructions, never allowed to restate a number the facts already give), and the facts stay exactly as pasteable as they were.

## Revised 2026-09-10 — Email/WhatsApp digests retired, the TriageList replaces message-by-message intake

lios#192: reading messages one at a time (Track C2's tiered Email/WhatsApp digests, and the old intake table's per-message rows) misread urgency twice in one session — a WhatsApp group question already answered later in the same thread surfaced as ~10 false "new" candidates, and a passing evening remark at the tail of an ordinary thread was elevated to "worth a check-in before bed." lios#193 folded in: the fix for both was the same shape Alex asked for directly — "what is useful to look at is stuff that's been explicitly sent to the inbox, and then we should look at conversations in context... here's a bunch of just FYI stuff, and then here are things where maybe we need to make a decision." Track C now builds that two-list **TriageList** from `inbox_pending` (List 1) and the new deterministic `conversations_since` (List 2, chat/thread grouping + a time-gap burst, no embedding call, no LLM call — see `app/integrations/system/conversations.py`), with only the FYI-vs-DECIDE label needing a (cheap, Haiku) judgement call. Track C2's `email`/`whatsapp` fragments are deleted; `## Conversations` in the note is built entirely from List 2. Persisting per-row skip state (the design's re-ask-once-then-drop default) is deferred to the next build step.
